                <pb facs="0838" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.001 L 76/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-06-16T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 16, 1922—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>148. Your 262 June 15, 8 P.M.</p>
                <p>Department approves suggested procedure merely to acknowledge receipt of note and
                    attend Li’s reception, thus dealing with the situation as a new administration
                    and not a new government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
